{"question_id": 66080996, "title": "Pyspark, PandasUDF; How to return a matrix using Pyspark.PandasUDF?", "question": "<p>I would like to implement a pandasUDF function in <code>PySpark</code> that returns a matrix of float numbers. I have tried, but the below appeared.</p>\n<pre><code>RuntimeError: ('Exception thrown when converting pandas.Series (float64) to \nArrow Array (list&lt;item: float&gt;). It can be caused by overflows or other\nunsafe conversions warned by Arrow. Arrow safe type check can be disabled by\nusing SQL config `spark.sql.execution.pandas.convertToArrowArraySafely`.',\nArrowNotImplementedError(&quot;NumPyConverter doesn't implement &lt;list&lt;item: float&gt;&gt;\nconversion. &quot;,))\n</code></pre>\n<p>I wonder if you have an idea to get a Spark DataFrame as the table below.</p>\n<p>Desired output:</p>\n<pre><code>+--------------------+--------------------+--------------------+\n|                  P0|                  P1|                  P2|\n+--------------------+--------------------+--------------------+\n|-6.384              |-2.950              |-2.095              |\n|-4.102              |-7.101              |-8.184              |\n|-1.614              |4.4842              |-10.00              |\n|-6.166              |-3.186              |-2.076              |\n.\n.\n.\n+--------------------+--------------------+--------------------+\n</code></pre>\n", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/66080996/pyspark-pandasudf-how-to-return-a-matrix-using-pyspark-pandasudf", "answer_id": 66126223, "answer": "<p>The answer is as follows:</p>\n<p>First:</p>\n<p>Converting the output into <code>StringType</code> as follow:</p>\n<pre><code>import pandas as pd\nfrom collections import Counter as Cs\nimport findspark\nfindspark.init()\nfrom pyspark import SparkContext\nfrom pyspark.sql.types import *\nfrom pyspark.sql.functions import udf, struct, pandas_udf, PandasUDFType\nimport pyspark.sql.functions as F\n\nstructList = []\nfor i in range(k):\n    structList.append(StructField('P' + str(i),\n            ArrayType(StringType()),\n            True))\nschema = StructType(structList) \n\n@pandas_udf(schema, PandasUDFType.GROUPED_MAP)\ndef apply_Func(data):\n    data = pd.DataFrame(data.astype(float).values[:,:-1])\n    label = someFunc(data.values,k,IR,i)\n    data['labels'] = label\n    leader = []\n    f = list(Cs(label))\n    f.sort()\n    for ii in f:\n        leader.append([round(np.mean(z), 10) for z in data[data['labels']==ii].\\\n               values[:, :-1].T])\n    cols = ['P'+str(i) for i in range(k)]\n    leader = pd.DataFrame(leader, columns=cols)\n    for c in cols:\n        leader[c] = leader[c].map(str)\n    return leader\n\ndf2.groupby('chunks').apply(apply_Func).show()\n</code></pre>\n<p>The output is as follows which in each element I have the character list of the float numbers.</p>\n<pre><code>+--------------------+--------------------+--------------------+\n|                  P0|                  P1|                  P2|\n+--------------------+--------------------+--------------------+\n|[-, 6, ., 3, 8, 4...|[-, 2, ., 9, 5, 0...|[-, 2, ., 0, 9, 5...|\n|[-, 4, ., 1, 0, 2...|[-, 7, ., 1, 0, 1...|[-, 8, ., 1, 8, 4...|\n|[-, 1, ., 6, 1, 4...|[4, ., 4, 8, 4, 2...|[-, 1, 0, ., 0, 0...|\n|[-, 6, ., 1, 6, 6...|[-, 3, ., 1, 8, 6...|[-, 2, ., 0, 7, 6...|\n|[-, 3, ., 9, 4, 2...|[-, 7, ., 1, 3, 8...|[-, 8, ., 1, 8, 7...|\n|[-, 1, ., 6, 4, 4...|[4, ., 4, 9, 9, 3...|[-, 9, ., 7, 3, 0...|\n|[-, 3, ., 7, 5, 5...|[-, 7, ., 0, 0, 7...|[-, 8, ., 3, 4, 3...|\n|[-, 6, ., 1, 0, 8...|[-, 3, ., 1, 7, 2...|[-, 2, ., 0, 4, 6...|\n|[-, 1, ., 9, 2, 4...|[4, ., 4, 2, 4, 9...|[-, 9, ., 9, 3, 2...|\n|[-, 4, ., 1, 1, 0...|[0, ., 5, 0, 0, 5...|[-, 5, ., 9, 3, 1...|\n|[-, 3, ., 7, 5, 5...|[-, 7, ., 2, 2, 4...|[-, 8, ., 1, 2, 7...|\n|[-, 0, ., 1, 9, 8...|[3, ., 8, 5, 3, 9...|[-, 1, 1, ., 1, 2...|\n|[-, 1, ., 6, 6, 1...|[4, ., 6, 5, 1, 5...|[-, 9, ., 9, 0, 6...|\n|[-, 3, ., 9, 0, 1...|[-, 7, ., 2, 4, 6...|[-, 8, ., 0, 6, 3...|\n|[-, 6, ., 1, 3, 7...|[-, 2, ., 9, 7, 3...|[-, 1, ., 9, 7, 3...|\n|[-, 6, ., 5, 5, 1...|[-, 2, ., 9, 5, 6...|[-, 2, ., 1, 7, 2...|\n|[-, 1, ., 5, 2, 9...|[4, ., 5, 2, 0, 9...|[-, 9, ., 9, 5, 9...|\n|[-, 4, ., 0, 2, 9...|[-, 7, ., 0, 5, 7...|[-, 8, ., 0, 9, 4...|\n|[-, 6, ., 5, 8, 1...|[-, 3, ., 0, 4, 0...|[-, 2, ., 1, 5, 4...|\n|[-, 3, ., 9, 4, 1...|[-, 6, ., 9, 6, 3...|[-, 8, ., 2, 0, 2...|\n+--------------------+--------------------+--------------------+\n</code></pre>\n<p>Second phase:</p>\n<p>Then turning the output into a normal matrix in the Pyspark:</p>\n<pre><code>for c in results.columns:\n    results = results.withColumn(c, F.array_join(c, &quot;&quot;))\nresults = results.select(*(col(c).cast(&quot;float&quot;).alias(c) for c in results.columns))\nresults.show()\n</code></pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre><code>+----------+----------+----------+\n|        P0|        P1|        P2|\n+----------+----------+----------+\n|-6.3002896|-3.1039708|-2.0802138|\n|-3.9664164|-6.9847507| -8.062131|\n|-1.8714522|  4.196398|-10.053752|\n|-1.4888309| 4.3933063|-10.096599|\n|-6.4817667|-3.1598282|-1.9742265|\n| -4.044648| -7.144871| -8.267062|\n|-1.7549628| 4.5405264| -9.912325|\n|-3.8847973|-7.0680466|  -7.91784|\n| -6.434804|-3.2674906|-1.9079945|\n|-1.7493968| 4.4715776| -9.837081|\n|-6.4625697|-3.0429673|-1.9384751|\n|-3.9936383|-7.1258874| -8.427638|\n|-3.8748856| -7.047747| -8.218606|\n|-1.6524452| 4.2945223| -9.954149|\n|-6.3087454|-3.1643403|-1.9838226|\n| -5.355266|-5.0064306|-4.5695004|\n| -2.995949|-7.3578677| -8.825416|\n|-1.6750498|  4.370491| -9.852942|\n| -1.511777| 4.3346696| -9.993404|\n| -5.128389| -4.756383|-4.7434697|\n+----------+----------+----------+\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code>results\nOutput:    DataFrame[P0: float, P1: float, P2: float]\n</code></pre>\n"}